## 7. Test execution reporting

After running tests, report:

- Exact command.
- Number of tests executed.
- Number passed.
- Number failed.
- Number skipped.
- Relevant failure details.
- Whether the test used mocks or the sandbox.

Never claim tests passed if they were not executed.

Never fabricate test output.

## 8. Final assignment verification

Maintain a checklist against all mandatory deliverables:

- Source code for M1–M4.
- GitHub repository and commit history.
- Working prototype.
- Database schema.
- API documentation.
- Architecture diagram.
- Sandbox evidence for each milestone.
- Screenshots or recording.
- API endpoints, callbacks and workflow documentation.
- Known issues and limitations.
- Setup and deployment instructions.
- AI usage documentation.
- Answers to all 15 technical questions.

Before final submission, identify every incomplete item honestly.
